<article class="env-definition" id="01BI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01BI">Definition <span data-tag="01BI">17.10.6</span>.</a> In the situation of Lemma <a href="/tag/01BH" data-tag="01BH">17.10.5</a> we say $\mathcal{F}_ M$ is the <em>sheaf associated to the module $M$ and the ring map $\alpha $</em>. If $R = \Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $\alpha = \text{id}_ R$ we simply say $\mathcal{F}_ M$ is the <em>sheaf associated to the module $M$</em>. </p>
